```python
def is_reasoning_block(block: Mapping[str, Any]) -> TypeGuard[ReasoningContentBlock]:
    """Check if a block is a ReasoningContentBlock."""
    return block.get("type") == "reasoning"


def is_text_block(block: Mapping[str, Any]) -> TypeGuard[TextContentBlock]:
    """Check if a block is a TextContentBlock."""
    return block.get("type") == "text"


def test_typing() -> None:
    """Test typing on things"""
    message = AIMessage(
        content="Hello",
    )
    if isinstance(message.content, str):
        # This should not raise an error
        message.content = message.content + " world"
    elif isinstance(message.content, list):
        all_contents = []
        for block in message.content:
            if isinstance(block, dict):
                if is_text_block(block):
                    all_contents.append(block["text"])
                if is_reasoning_block(block):
                    all_contents.append(block.get("reasoning", "foo"))
```

ChatOpenAI's treatment of the Responses API requires an update. It currently stores reasoning, built-in tool calls/outputs, and other items in `additional_kwargs`, generating AIMessages of the form:
```python
AIMessage(
    content=[
        {"type": "text", "text": "Hello, world!", "annotations": [{"type": "foo"}]}
    ],
    additional_kwargs={
        "reasoning": {
            "type": "reasoning",
            "id": "rs_123",
            "summary": [{"type": "summary_text", "text": "Reasoning summary"}],
        },
        "tool_outputs": [
            {"type": "web_search_call", "id": "websearch_123", "status": "completed"}
        ],
    },
    response_metadata={"id": "resp_123"},
    id="msg_123",
)
```
There are several issues associated with this:
- We don't accommodate the case where the Response contains multiple message items— we only store a single message ID and lose the association between text blocks and message items
- We lose all but one of the reasoning items
- We lose the sequencing of items.

This introduces issues in some contexts, primarily under zero data retention, which requires reconstructing Response objects from AIMessages.

Here we refactor ChatOpenAI so that internally we represent Response items in the content sequence:
```python
AIMessage(
    content=[
        {
            "type": "reasoning",
            "summary": [{"type": "summary_text", "text": "Reasoning summary"}],
            "id": "rs_123",
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hello, world!",
            "annotations": [{"type": "foo"}],
            "id": "msg_123",
        },
        {"type": "web_search_call", "id": "websearch_123", "status": "completed"},
    ],
    response_metadata={"id": "resp_123"},
    id="resp_123",
)
```
This representation is consistent with other providers (e.g., ChatAnthropic and ChatVertexAI).

We add functions to translate to/from these representations so that there are no changes in behavior.

A subsequent PR will enable users to opt-in to the updated representation.

